{"title":"2009 Polish Mathematical Olympiad Third Round","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Polish_Mathematical_Olympiad_Third_Round&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Polish_Mathematical_Olympiad_Third_Round&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Each of the vertices of a convex hexagon is a center of a circle of radius equal to the not longer side of the hexagon which includes that vertex. Prove that if the common part of all six circles (including the edge) is not empty, then the hexagon is regular.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Polish_Mathematical_Olympiad_Third_Round&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of all points of the plane with integer coordinates. Find the smallest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that there exists subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> with the following property: For any two different elements <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f642cbbd390b4882363ab6b5c2906dbf6be6cc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> of that subset there exists a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66d6baaeabf47f953db9449050e0dab66474153e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> such that the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Polish_Mathematical_Olympiad_Third_Round&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/f/3efd92d7eef6e4b04b61b6ff7e353462a2607585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P,Q,R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" /> be polynomials of degree at least one, with real coefficients, satisfying for all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> the equalities <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb38aa07f6508241f31eaf01f6674cd21bdb4611.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(Q(x)) = Q(R(x)) = R(P(x)).\\]\" width=\"252\" height=\"18\" /> Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/8/bf8264ca93316f2013d5cb4b7c7e95efb47f68a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=Q=R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Polish_Mathematical_Olympiad_Third_Round&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Polish_Mathematical_Olympiad_Third_Round&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae21bd4bf9cee6f09b70d1f0af125fca9174fa0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" /> be nonnegative numbers with sum equal to 1. Prove that there exist numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/0/5408db57890f657fa9b071dffde77d30cc4eb280.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n \\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"221\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d771aecf6574ee728e7cbfacefa7df0da30b655a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n) \\neq (2,2,\\ldots,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"231\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/2/fb28407d0f0bbba36d5fcbe0b465c39c138b0d03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\leq a_1x_1 + a_2x_2 + \\ldots + a_nx_n \\leq 2 + \\frac{2}{3^n - 1}\\]\" width=\"335\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Polish_Mathematical_Olympiad_Third_Round&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Sphere inscribed in tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to its sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a4545bd933ba641bfecaf49baf13a9ebfd38b29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD,ACD,ABD,ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"198\" height=\"16\" /> respectively in points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/2/532a24574d3d201d320393c77a192198111629bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P,Q,R,S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />. The segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2ebdc03b4e24dbee7b5747d6a0aa2def18f5541d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PT$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> is the diameter of that sphere and points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/2418852400ca72247fbe556064b4777e7a7683e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;,Q&#39;,R&#39;,S&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"19\" /> are the intersections of  lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb0b2d58093ab2c5f7843cf56a0aeef1d81d6d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TA,TQ,TR,TS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" /> with the plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7ada763e99852a6e44a15d46cce3c3709a944d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> is the center of the circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3ae693f7e5dac8d7685df699431977891f14371d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q&#39;R&#39;S&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Polish_Mathematical_Olympiad_Third_Round&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e6a2d706867d6652d7edadccc3fd034130bd98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> be a natural number. The sequence of nonnegative numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/e/13ebbce5f9dedb2cd202dbdd153a9aa7663bd9e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(c_0,c_1, \\ldots, c_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" /> satisfies the condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c4918b6865050ca3249ba822c8e9d84ce406314.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c_pc_s + c_rc_t = c_{p+r}c_{r+s}\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"16\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef43ada0209d7033b62c025e745e6a35672d8281.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p,r,s,t \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"17\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55b79fb06e8b707e136b87c9c3b41f137f4c8c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+r+s+t = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"17\" />. Find all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d4142d351ef99cc26a94e44c1912d904dd4a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/c/16c28fe4e4d9b723f59b9d3eb799a9a5864aa38e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018022919\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.028 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 164/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5614/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22884:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018022919 and revision id 175595. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}